# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 014 — supersedes gap-008
# Act: INS*  (Instance aimed at Pattern)   Stance: Composing   Site: Kind
#
# gap-008 refused this act for lack of a second anchor to compose with.
# That gap is superseded, not deleted — turn-12 and turn-13 each anchored
# one member of the kind individually, so two independent anchors now
# exist: @f1292533... (signal-a) and @14ba529c... (signal-b). Composed —
# SHA-256 over the sorted pair — into a new, third anchor:
#
#   @a1b3b873bc22f48073387ef56c61172c00b06332a179e453349766dbef2dfa2f
#
# The honest finding, checked and not assumed: this composed anchor is
# NOT identical to turn-7's kind-anchor (@444b54f3...). Recorded plainly
# rather than treated as a failure, because it isn't one — the two
# anchors were built by different constructions. Turn-7's anchor hashes
# the kind's SHARED PROPERTIES directly (site-role, sign, membership,
# control) with no reference to the members' own identities. This turn's
# anchor hashes the MEMBERS' identities together, with no direct reference
# to the shared properties. Content-addressing is sensitive to exactly
# what was hashed, not to what a reader takes the hash to mean — two
# anchors can point at genuinely related territory without being the same
# entity, and pretending otherwise would be exactly the kind of claim
# SIG's mutable sign is for, not INS's rigid one. There are now, correctly
# and by construction, TWO anchors for two different (related) entities:
# "the kind, described directly" (turn-7) and "the kind, arrived at by
# composing its members" (this turn) — SYN's job, when this kernel reaches
# it, is exactly to decide whether and how those should relate; INS's job
# stops at minting each honestly, which it has now done for both paths.
#
# Earning argument: precondition was two independent anchors to compose —
# satisfied by turn-12 and turn-13, both individually earned against their
# own targets' evidence, not against each other. Refuted if the composed
# digest could not be independently reproduced from anchor-002.json and
# anchor-003.json alone — checked directly, reproduces exactly.

:turn-14  eot:opens        :turn-13 .
:turn-14  eot:supersedes   :gap-008 .
:turn-14  eot:act          eot:INS* .
:turn-14  eot:stance       "Composing" .
:turn-14  eot:site         "Kind" .
:turn-14  eot:composes     "@f1292533ea4f49108d50bb02e4f2b56e5f62bbdd0686ad9728739b7c2c8aec3e" .
:turn-14  eot:composes     "@14ba529c7c6548b018aa4302dac0e84c97102ee043b421db4c734c3daec2d0d6" .
:turn-14  eot:mints        "@a1b3b873bc22f48073387ef56c61172c00b06332a179e453349766dbef2dfa2f" .
:turn-14  eot:distinct_from  :turn-7 .
:turn-14  eot:witnessed    true .
:turn-14  eot:closes       [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
